ct token, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"type":"text","text":", one object per record, oldest first, with these members:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s stored properties, by name, then the members listed below","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked: ISO 8601 in UTC, with milliseconds ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2026-11-23T14:03:27.512Z"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"uuid","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent, and every event is anonymous: ","type":"text"},{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$process_person_profile: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so PostHog makes no person profile, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$geoip_disable: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so PostHog doesn’t add a location from the request’s IP address. A record with no session (one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") is its own anonymous person, linked to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing: PostHog rejects a whole batch when one of its events has no ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A record a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out under the ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its first send. PostHog counts a person per ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so its unique users","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are sessions. The session is also sent as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which PostHog’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sessions and web analytics group events by (","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the UUIDv7 they require); a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with no session has none. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context value, aren’t sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property whose name starts with "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which only a hand-written "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write, or is "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", is left out and logged at notice level, as PostHog reads those"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names as settings ("},{"code":"$set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$process_person_profile","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") or the identity."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$app_namespace","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_build","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundle identifier, version and build, each left out when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$device_type","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mobile"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tablet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Desktop"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TV"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vision"},{"type":"text","text":" for the form factor; no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_type"},{"type":"text","text":" for a watch"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"$locale","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$network_wifi"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$network_cellular"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi, and whether it is cellular"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The operating system’s name and version","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a name PostHog keeps for its own events), one whose event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for PostHog to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. PostHog answers a batch it takes with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"200, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" retries one that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it rejects. A record sent again keeps its "},{"code":"uuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/PostHogEncodingError":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PostHogEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PostHogEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PostHogEncodingError","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/posthogencodingerror","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s requests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no record of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncodi